      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Here. When LAP is enabled, the lookahead buffer is a linear buffer. When LAP is not enable, it is a circular buffer, so there is no OOB issue.\n\u003e See line 1000, the stats of a new buffer will always be written to the end of the lookahead buffer, and the buffer pointer increases every frame.\n\u003e So when we set a small lookahead buffer size, it will quickly go the the end.\n\u003e If we don\u0027t clamp it, it will go out of bounds.\n\nI guess I\u0027m wondering if we\u0027ll be looking at the correct stats in that case.",
