      "lineNbr": 1005,
      "author": {
        "id": 6585
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-28T19:27:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "lag-in-frames determines the size of look-ahead stats buffers. In the first pass mode, this stats buffer linearly increments. So the when the number of frames is larger than the lag-in-frames size, OOB will happen. It means, it can not be properly fixed unless stats buffer is circular or compacted since the number of frames can increase to a very large number but lag-in-frames can not.\n\nIn the stats analysis stage, a minimum of MAX_GF_LENGTH_LAP (16) is required to not break the existing logic.\n\nSo in the new patch, I allocate at least MAX_GF_LENGTH_LAP + 1 for stats buffer size even if lag-in-frames is smaller.\n\nAlso, I use a compact window size to avoid stats buffer goes out of boundary.\n\nPlease take another look.",
      "parentUuid": "a2da032e_ef7f93cb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1004,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 1005,
        "endChar": 56
      },
